# Fractal Glass — a draggable orange circle (an invisible RN view drives cx/cy) seen through a 4x4 "fractal glass" panel: inside the panel it is blurred and alpha-masked by gradient tiles; a sun/moon button cross-fades the light/dark theme.
# What this test covers: dragging the circle from above the panel into its centre, across tile seams, half in/half
# out of every panel edge, back out, a fast fling, re-grabbing it after each move (pan context), and toggling the
# theme (background + circle colour timings) once, back, and rapidly while dragging.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/fractal-glass"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait 1200
# From its start (180,270) into the middle of the glass.
gesture pan 180 270 20 170 800
wait 600
# Across tile seams.
gesture pan 200 440 -100 0 600
gesture pan 100 440 200 0 900
gesture pan 300 440 -100 -80 600
wait 500
# Straddle each panel edge (top y=287, bottom y=587, left x=40, right x=362).
gesture pan 200 360 0 -80 500
wait 300
gesture pan 200 280 0 300 800
wait 300
gesture pan 200 580 -160 -140 700
wait 300
gesture pan 40 440 322 0 800
wait 300
# Back out above the panel and fast fling back into it.
gesture pan 362 440 -180 -230 500
wait 300
gesture pan 182 210 20 230 120
wait 600
# Theme to dark and back.
press 309 781
wait 800
press 309 781
wait 800
# Toggle to dark, drag during the cross-fade, rapid toggles.
press 309 781
gesture pan 202 440 -30 40 500
press 309 781 --count 4 --interval-ms 120
wait 1200
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
